---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'; import ProductCard from '../components/ProductCard.astro'; import { products } from '../data/products';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title="Foresight Labs · Thoughtful software for everyday intelligence." description="Foresight Labs creates refined digital products that turn complex information into calm, useful and human-centred experiences.">
  <section class="home-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Independent product studio · 2026</p><h1>Thoughtful software<br />for everyday <em>intelligence.</em></h1><div class="hero-intro"><p>Foresight Labs creates refined digital products that turn complex information into calm, useful and human-centred experiences.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-dark" href={`${base}products/`}>Explore our products ↗</a><a class="text-link" href={`${base}about/`}>About the studio</a></div></div><div class="hero-meta"><div>Based in<strong>India · Working independently</strong></div><div>What we value<strong>Clarity · Care · Curiosity</strong></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container studio-lede"><p class="eyebrow">A quieter kind of progress</p><h2>Technology should leave more room for being human.</h2><p>We make products for the moments when information becomes overwhelming, routines become complicated, or the important thing is simply hard to see. Our work pairs practical technology with considered interfaces and responsible intelligence.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section section-tint"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Selected work</p><h2>Made with intention.</h2></div><p>Three products, each exploring a different way thoughtful software can support everyday life.</p></div><div class="product-grid">{products.map((product) => <ProductCard product={product} />)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Our principles</p><h2>Small signals.<br /><em>Better systems.</em></h2></div><p>Good design is a way of paying attention. These are the ideas we return to when the answer is not obvious.</p></div><div class="principles"><div class="principle"><span>01</span><h3>Make it calm</h3><p>Interfaces should reduce cognitive load, not add to it.</p></div><div class="principle"><span>02</span><h3>Earn trust</h3><p>Be honest about what a system knows, does and does not do.</p></div><div class="principle"><span>03</span><h3>Keep learning</h3><p>Build with curiosity, then leave enough room to change.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="cta-band"><div class="container cta-content"><div><p class="eyebrow">Have a thoughtful idea?</p><h2>Let’s make room<br /><em>for it.</em></h2></div><a class="button button-dark" href={`${base}contact/`}>Start a conversation ↗</a></div></section>
</Layout>
